hifiberry-auth (0.2.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Signing out no longer clears the session cookie when it refuses the
    request. It used to clear it on both branches while deleting the session
    only on success, so a client whose CSRF token had gone stale lost the
    cookie to the 401 and could not retry: the browser ended up signed out
    while the session stayed valid on the device.
  * Setting the protection policy now requires a CSRF token, like every other
    write. protection=off unprotects the whole device, so it was the one
    damaging write a session cookie alone could perform.
  * A CSRF token containing non-ASCII characters is refused with a 401 instead
    of raising and returning a 500.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 18:55:59 +0000

hifiberry-auth (0.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Sign-out now ends the session. POST /api/auth/logout previously cleared
    the caller's cookie and nothing else; because sessions were stateless the
    token stayed valid until its own expiry, up to thirty days. A kept copy of
    the cookie still authenticated after a proper sign-out.
  * Session ids are recorded in an allowlist table; a cookie is accepted only
    while its row exists. Logout deletes one row.
  * Changing the device password ends every other session.
  * Logout requires a valid session and a matching CSRF token, like every
    other write.
  * Sessions established before this version stop being accepted, so every
    device signs in once after the upgrade.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 16:38:26 +0000

hifiberry-auth (0.1.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Restart on manifest changes via a dpkg trigger on /etc/hifiberry/auth.d.
    Manifests were only read at startup and nothing restarted the service when
    a package shipped one, so on a fresh install hifiberry-auth came up as a
    dependency before configurator and audiocontrol dropped theirs, classified
    every endpoint as risky and 401'd the entire web UI.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-auth (0.1.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Version bump only. Supersedes an ad-hoc 0.1.1 build (argon2 exception
    portability fix) that was never recorded in this changelog, so the released
    package version stays ahead of anything already deployed. The argon2 fix is
    included.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-auth (0.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: session + password store, classification manifests, the
    nginx auth_request verify endpoint, and the auth API.

